Problem: Car Rental Management System

Imagine a local car rental company is still using spreadsheets and WhatsApp messages to track cars and customers. They want a backend API to manage everything.

The Problem

The company needs a system that can:

Store all cars in the fleet.
Track whether a car is available, rented, or under maintenance.
Store customer information.
Allow customers to rent cars.
Record when cars are returned.
Generate reports of active rentals.
Main Entities

Car
{
    make: "Toyota",
    model: "Corolla",
    year: 2022,
    plateNumber: "AS-1234-25",
    dailyRate: 150,
    status: "available"
}
Customer
{
    name: "John Doe",
    email: "john@gmail.com",
    phone: "0240000000",
    licenseNumber: "DL123456"
}
Rental
{
    customerId: "...",
    carId: "...",
    startDate: "2026-05-31",
    endDate: "2026-06-05",
    totalCost: 750,
    status: "active"
}
API Requirements
Cars

Create Car

POST /api/cars

Get All Cars

GET /api/cars

Get Single Car

GET /api/cars/:id

Update Car

PATCH /api/cars/:id

Delete Car

DELETE /api/cars/:id
Customers

Create Customer

POST /api/customers

Get Customers

GET /api/customers

Get One Customer

GET /api/customers/:id
Rentals

Rent a Car

POST /api/rentals

Request Body

{
    "customerId": "...",
    "carId": "...",
    "days": 5
}

Business Rules:

Car must exist.
Customer must exist.
Car status must be available.
Calculate total cost automatically.
Change car status to rented.

Return a Car

POST /api/rentals/:id/return

Business Rules:

Rental must exist.
Rental must be active.
Change rental status to returned.
Change car status to available.